      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Todd,\n\nMoving the connect_lock outside usb_udc struct (KMI type). This implies that the lock would be common to all usb_udc instances (one per udc controller instance) instead of having one per udc controller instance. A minor tradeoff in performance in the interest of the code thread safe (to solve a race). Hoping that this solves the KMI breakage.\n\nWould this be OK ?\n\nOne a different note, say if this patch comes from linux-5.10.y as is, would it still come under the purview of KMI breakage ?",
